sequenceDiagram
    participant Client as External Client
    participant Router as OpenShift Router<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant Gateway as Data Science Gateway<br/>(Envoy) 443/TCP HTTPS
    participant KRBP as kube-rbac-proxy<br/>8443/TCP HTTPS<br/>TLS (serving cert)
    participant K8sAPI as Kubernetes API<br/>6443/TCP HTTPS
    participant REST as rest-container<br/>8080/TCP HTTP
    participant DB as PostgreSQL/MySQL<br/>5432/3306/TCP
    participant Operator as Model Registry Operator

    rect rgb(240, 248, 255)
        Note over Client,DB: Flow 1: REST API Request via OpenShift Route
        Client->>Router: POST /v1/model_registry/{name}/...<br/>HTTPS/443, TLS (edge)
        Router->>KRBP: Forward request<br/>HTTPS/8443, TLS reencrypt (serving cert)
        KRBP->>K8sAPI: SubjectAccessReview<br/>HTTPS/6443, TLS, SA token
        K8sAPI-->>KRBP: Allowed (services/get check)
        KRBP->>REST: Forward (proxy-authorized)<br/>HTTP/8080, localhost
        REST->>DB: Query/Mutation<br/>PostgreSQL/5432 or MySQL/3306<br/>Configurable SSL, Password auth
        DB-->>REST: Result set
        REST-->>KRBP: Response
        KRBP-->>Router: HTTPS Response
        Router-->>Client: HTTPS Response
    end

    rect rgb(255, 248, 240)
        Note over Client,DB: Flow 2: REST API Request via Gateway API (HTTPRoute)
        Client->>Gateway: POST /model-registry/{name}/...<br/>HTTPS/443, TLS, Platform auth
        Gateway->>KRBP: HTTPRoute path-prefix routing<br/>HTTPS/8443, TLS
        KRBP->>K8sAPI: SubjectAccessReview<br/>HTTPS/6443, TLS, SA token
        K8sAPI-->>KRBP: Allowed
        KRBP->>REST: Forward (proxy-authorized)<br/>HTTP/8080, localhost
        REST->>DB: Query/Mutation<br/>Configurable SSL
        DB-->>REST: Result set
        REST-->>KRBP: Response
        KRBP-->>Gateway: HTTPS Response
        Gateway-->>Client: HTTPS Response
    end

    rect rgb(240, 255, 240)
        Note over Operator,K8sAPI: Flow 3: Operator Reconcile Loop
        K8sAPI->>Operator: Watch event (ModelRegistry CR change)<br/>HTTPS, TLS, SA token
        Operator->>K8sAPI: Get/Create/Update/Delete resources<br/>HTTPS/6443, TLS, SA token
        Note right of Operator: Creates: Deployment, Service,<br/>SA, RBAC, Route, HTTPRoute,<br/>NetworkPolicy, Group, PVC
        Operator->>K8sAPI: Read OpenShift config<br/>(ingress domain, TLS profile)
        K8sAPI-->>Operator: Cluster configuration
    end
